-- title:
--   Inertial semilinear action on the Drinfeld chart with diagonal linear part
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and assume $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the subgroup $H_1 = \mathrm{ker}\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\big) \cap \mathrm{ker}\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times\big)$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$ ([`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$). Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring, a domain with $L$ as fraction field, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the coefficientwise image in $L$ of the $q$-expansion $\mathsf{q}^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{num}}$ of the modular $j$-function, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Write $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin A K j` (the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$) and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf A K j` (the elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$) along the middle chart.
--
--   Let $z$ be a point of $X$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism `TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase A K j` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$; it is assumed that $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk of $X$ at $z$, so $z$ lies over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $y$ be a point of $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin A K j` with `ιFin` mapping $y$ to $z$. The supersingularity hypothesis `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A K j` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $\bar{j}$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\bar{j}$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Chart data: $W$ is a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal), $\sigma : A \to W$ a ring homomorphism with $\sigma(\varpi)$ generating the maximal ideal of $W$; $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^{q} - X_0^{q}X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)); and $e$ is a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ for its maximal ideal onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma\varpi)\,v - f\,u)$. Throughout, $\mathrm{STK}$ denotes the stalk at $z$, $\mathrm{CMP}$ its adic completion, $\mathrm{toC} : \mathrm{STK} \to \mathrm{CMP}$ the canonical map, $\mathrm{mkS} : W[[X_0,X_1]] \to S$ the quotient map, and $\mathrm{germY}$ the ring homomorphism from `chartAlgFin A K j` to $\mathrm{STK}$ obtained from the identification of the global sections of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with `chartAlgFin A K j` followed by the germ at $z$ on the open image of `ιFin`.
--
--   Three further hypotheses on this chart witness are imposed.
--
--   (`hconst`, constants) For every $a \in A$, the isomorphism $e$ carries the image in $\mathrm{CMP}$ of the germ at $z$ of $a$ (pulled back through `toBase`) to $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma a))$.
--
--   (`hlin`, equivariant linear parts) For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f_0, g_0$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, $p_g$ having nonzero image, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the Laurent expansion of $\tau x$ pushed through $\iota$ times the $q$-expansion of $g_0 \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f_0 \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ — and for every proof that $\tau$ maps `chartAlgFin A K j` into itself, if the induced endomorphism of `chartAlgFin A K j` is the identity modulo the prime of $y$, then there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ such that: $\theta$ intertwines $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ with $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ precomposed with the restriction of $\tau$; $\theta$ fixes all constants $\mathrm{mkS}(C\,w)$; for each $j'$, $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_{j'})) - \mathrm{mkS}\big(\sum_{i} C(M_{i j'})X_i\big)$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0), \mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$; $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$ for all $i,j$; if $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ then $c \equiv 1$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$; and if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c - 1$ is not in the maximal ideal of $W$.
--
--   (`hanchor`, anchored branch) For every prime ideal $P$ of $S$ with $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0) \notin P$ or $\mathrm{mkS}(X_1) \notin P$, containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))$, and containing an element of the form $\mathrm{mkS}(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a$ in `chartAlgFin A K j`: the image $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ lies in the preimage of $P$ under $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ is the image of an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   Conclusion. For every $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, every ring automorphism $\sigma_L$ of $L$ and every ring automorphism $\sigma_A$ of $A$ such that $\sigma_L$ and $\sigma_A$ agree under $A \to L$, such that $\sigma_A(a) - a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ for all $a \in A$, and such that $\sigma_L(\zeta) = \zeta^{\,\mathrm{val}(d)}$, and for every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ acting coefficientwise through $\sigma_L$ (the Laurent expansion of $\tau x$ is [`ModularCurve.coeffMap`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) of $\sigma_L$ applied to that of $x$), the following hold.
--
--   First, $\tau$ maps `chartAlgFin A K j` into itself.
--
--   Second, for every proof `hpres` of that preservation: the restriction of $\tau$ to `chartAlgFin A K j` is the identity modulo the prime ideal of $y$, i.e. $\tau(a) - a$ lies in the prime of $y$ for all $a$ in the chart algebra; and there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a ring automorphism $\sigma_W$ of $W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ such that
--
--   1. $\theta\big(e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a)))\big) = e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\tau a)))$ for every $a$ in `chartAlgFin A K j`, $\tau$ being taken in its restricted form;
--
--   2. $\sigma_W(\sigma a) = \sigma(\sigma_A a)$ for every $a \in A$;
--
--   3. $\sigma_W(w) - w$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$ for every $w \in W$;
--
--   4. $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(C\,w)) = \mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_W w))$ for every $w \in W$, so $\theta$ is $\sigma_W$-semilinear on constants;
--
--   5. for each $j'$, $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_{j'})) - \mathrm{mkS}\big(\sum_{i} C(M_{i j'})X_i\big)$ lies in the square of the ideal of $S$ generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0)$ and $\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$;
--
--   6. for all $i, j'$, the difference $M_{i j'} - \big(\mathrm{val}\big(d \cdot (\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^{q})^{-1})_{i j'}\big)\big)_W$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$, where [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.diagOneElem q (d ^ q)⁻¹`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L233) is the matrix $\mathrm{diag}(1, (d^{q})^{-1})$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$, its entries are multiplied by $d$ in $\mathbb{Z}/q$, and each resulting element of $\mathbb{Z}/q$ is sent to $W$ via its natural-number representative. Thus the linear part of $\theta$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $W$ to the diagonal matrix with entries $d$ and $d^{1-q}$.
--
--   This is the inertia step in the analysis of the local structure of the integral model of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ at a supersingular point of the fibre over $q$, where the Drinfeld equation $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ describes the crossing: an automorphism of $K$ acting coefficientwise by a cyclotomic character value $d$ is shown to act on the completed stalk, through the chart isomorphism $e$, by a $\sigma_W$-semilinear automorphism whose linear part is the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(d, d^{1-q})$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_of_levelAut_riders_inertia_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_of_levelAut_riders_inertia_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd), which packages the chart together with its level and inertia equivariance.
